From: VIctory contributor <contributor@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:33:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 34/43] GPU: VICTORY_BACK_QUIET=1 (hand port of fork #1188; NOT
 YET COMPILED)

A copy-back's own write into private, write-watched title memory reads
as a title write at the next refresh, and the copy takes its own output
in again. With VICTORY_BACK_QUIET=1 (off by default) the write is made
as before, the kernel's write-watch bits of its pages are reset (only if
none was set before the write), the journal is told (watch::wrote_own)
so other copies take the pages, and the writing copy notes itself
current.

Hand port: fork #1188 (0460bf53) sits on the fork's own-view copy-back
(put_back_own, shaders_write), which this line does not have, so only
BACK_QUIET is taken; BACK_OWN_VIEW is not separable from that work.
Sites: the one write per copy in copy_back_with, and the changed runs of
relay_merge, card_merge and card_merge_relay (Shadow::write_runs).

Written in a read-only window: not compiled, not tested. Build and
test before any use.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
